.TH FSVR 1 "2026-10-26" "de-xr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fsvr \- explore files in a native spatial browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
fsvr [\-\-layout map|tree|disc] [PATH]
fsvr \-\-model-xr FILE [\-\-seconds N] [\-\-report FILE]
fsvr \-\-model-render FILE OUTPUT.ppm [\-\-seconds N]
fsvr \-\-version
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The default CMake build uses patched FLTK 1.4.5 and OpenGL. It offers list and
spatial views, MapV/TreeV/DiscV layouts, ray picking, tabs/history, an inspector,
asynchronous file operations and archive browsing/extraction/compression.
Multiple path operands open separate tabs.
.PP
Qt6/Vulkan is a separate frontend, explicitly selected with
.BR \-DDE_XR_TOOLKIT=Qt6 .
Meson currently builds the Qt frontend only. Qt-specific routing options and
standalone XR must not be assumed for the default FLTK executable.
.SH FLTK OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-layout " map|tree|disc
Select initial spatial layout; default map.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print build identity without opening a window. Supply it as the first argument.
.TP
.BI "\-\-smoke\-test " OUTPUT.png
Render a diagnostic capture and scene image, print a summary, and exit.
The argument is a filename, not a duration.
.TP
.B \-\-xr, \-\-openxr
Report that standalone OpenXR is not ported and exit with an error.
Launch through DomeD's XR application launcher instead.
.PP
--help describes the native command line. --desktop is accepted for DomeD launcher
compatibility. FLTK does not implement Qt's --domed, --select or --properties
CLI flags. Use the corresponding interface commands where available.
.TP
.B \-\-model-probe
Print model-overlay XR availability as JSON without opening a desktop window.
.TP
.BI "\-\-model-xr " FILE
Open a stereoscopic glTF/GLB overlay above the existing XR session.
Optional --seconds N limits duration (zero means unlimited); --report FILE
writes diagnostics. Requires OpenGL/EGL and XR_EXTX_overlay support.
.TP
.BI "\-\-model-render " "FILE OUTPUT.ppm"
Capture the model using native EGL. Optional --seconds N selects animation time.
.SH LIVE GLTF PREVIEW
Open a local glTF or GLB file, or choose File / Live glTF preview.
Drag to orbit, wheel to zoom, middle/Shift-drag to pan, R to reset.
The preview offers animation selection, playback, Orbit and Open in XR.
Models, buffers and PNG/JPEG textures reload after edits; malformed reloads
retain the last usable object. Loading and filesystem scans run in background
workers. Resource limits and unsupported required extensions report errors.
Archive members must first be extracted with their resources.
.PP
In XR, squeeze either grip near the object or while aiming at it to grab.
Move/turn a held controller to move/turn the object. Hold both grips to scale
and rotate around their midpoint. Release to leave it in place.
Left X resets placement; right B closes the overlay. Tracking/focus loss
releases grabs and requires a fresh press. Touch/Quest bindings are the default.
.SH FLTK CONTROLS
Left-click selects; double-click or Enter opens. Right-drag orbits the scene;
a short right-click opens actions. Middle-drag or Shift+left-drag pans;
the wheel zooms. Keys 1, 2 and 3 select MapV, TreeV and DiscV; F6 toggles spatial view.
.PP
In a DomeD session, application commands appear in the universal menu; the
duplicate in-window menu bar is hidden and its keyboard shortcuts remain active.
Spatial folder selection updates the side list. The sidebar and spatial viewport
remain separate when resizing the window or toggling the spatial view.
.PP
Ctrl+T opens a tab, Ctrl+W closes it, and Ctrl+Enter opens the selection in a new
tab. Alt+Left/Right navigate history, Alt+Up opens the parent and Alt+Home opens
home. F5 refreshes. F2 renames, Delete moves to Trash and Alt+Enter shows properties.
Ctrl+C/X/V copy, cut and paste; Ctrl+Shift+C copies the location;
Ctrl+A selects all, Ctrl/Shift+click toggles/ranges the list selection;
Ctrl+D bookmarks the current folder. Ctrl+Shift+N creates a folder.
Super+W closes the window; Super+Q quits.
.SH PLACES, TRASH AND FILE TRANSFERS
.SS SMB / Samba
Enter smb://server/ to list shares or smb://server/share/folder to connect directly.
Go / Connect to SMB server opens the native connection flow. Authentication uses
FLTK username/domain and masked-password controls; credentials are never stored
in bookmarks or command arguments. The headless GVfs SMB and FUSE backends provide
user-session filesystem access for normal file operations and previews.
Go / Disconnect SMB share performs a normal unmount without forcing busy clients.
SMB bookmarks reconnect using stable URLs. Other remote schemes are unsupported.
.PP
Places lists Home, XDG user directories, Trash, File System and local GTK/Dolphin
bookmarks. Go / Add bookmark and Remove bookmark manage FSVR's own bookmarks.
The location trash:/// opens the current user's home and mounted-volume Trash.
Restore from Trash returns selected items to their original existing parent
directories, refusing collisions. Delete permanently and Empty Trash ask for
confirmation. Damaged metadata can prevent restoration; such entries remain deletable.
.PP
Native Wayland and X11 file clipboard formats support cross-application copy/cut/paste.
Left-drag selected files from the list or spatial view to copy. Drop onto a spatial
folder or the current file area. Dragging always copies; use Cut/Paste to move.
Transfers run in the background, support cancellation, and offer Keep both, Skip
or Cancel on conflicts. Files already completed remain after cancellation.
Remote URLs and remote bookmark mounting are not supported.
.SH SORTING
View / Sort by and folder context menus offer natural Name, Size, Modified,
Type, Created, Accessed and Extension ordering, ascending/descending,
folders first and case-sensitive names. Sibling ordering is shared by all three
spatial layouts and retains selection. Unknown dates stay last; creation dates
need statx support. Preferences are saved in the FLTK settings file.
.SH XR AND APPEARANCE
DomeD supplies the GPU Wayland/XR surface and ordinary mouse/keyboard seat;
it owns the headset session. Application menus are exported through
DBusMenu/KDE AppMenu where supported. DomeD palette and native bitmap strikes
update live with the required FLTK patches. Native glTF overlays support motion
controllers; standalone filesystem-scene hands/controllers are not ported.
Accessibility/IME, bitmap shaping/bidi and broad
fractional-scale coverage also remain incomplete.
.SH ARCHIVES AND PREVIEWS
All libarchive readers/filters are enabled. Browse or extract ZIP, 7-Zip, tar,
CPIO, ar/deb, RPM, ISO, XAR, WARC, RAR, CAB, LHA and compressed streams as supported
by the selected runtime. Compress provides a format chooser; ZIP creation can
use an AES-256 password. Extract to chooses a new destination; Extract selected
limits extraction to a member/subtree. Operations report progress and can cancel.
Existing destinations, traversal, escaping links and special files are refused.
Reader/writer errors remove partial output. Relative links, normal permissions
and timestamps are preserved. Password prompts do not write passwords to disk.
.PP
Image cards use bounded background thumbnails rather than full-resolution image
loads. Folder changes cancel queued work and drop stale results. JPEG downscales
in the decoder; PNG/GIF use scanlines and BMP samples rows. The optional Qt
provider also bounds image and thumbnail-cache decoding. Model textures retain
separate explicit resource limits; hidden passive models follow selection.
.PP
fsvr-dome-default --archives-only selects fsvr for Dome archive handling without
changing folder/trash choices or other desktop sessions. Multiple local file URLs
open separate tabs. New DomeD settings rows appear in the next session.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fsvr/fltk.json
FLTK sorting settings; the default configuration root is ~/.config.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fsvr/places
FSVR's local bookmarks. GTK and Dolphin bookmarks are also imported.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dome/appearance.json
DomeD appearance settings.
.PP
The retained Qt frontend separately uses user-places.xbel for Places and
$XDG_CACHE_HOME/fsvr/index-v1 for its revalidated preview index.
Those are not documented FLTK feature parity.
.SH QT FRONTEND
Qt provides --desktop, --domed, --select, --properties and --help options.
Its --xr requires a build with Qt Quick 3D XR and an active OpenXR runtime;
inside DomeD use its ordinary launch rather than a second session.
Its --smoke-test is a timed diagnostic flag, unlike the FLTK filename option.
See the repository README for Qt-specific controls and filesystem behavior.
.SH INSTALLATION
Build Release as a regular user, using the matching patched FLTK 1.4.5 runtime.
The FLTK CMake target installs its executable, desktop entry, archive MIME
definitions, fsvr-dome-default helper, manual and dependency notices.
A private libarchive 3.8.10+ can be staged under /usr/local/lib/fsvr.
Review staged files before privileged system installation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
fsvr "$HOME"
fsvr --layout tree /path/to/directory
fsvr --layout disc /path/to/archive.zip
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dome\-compositor (1),
.BR qimgvr (1)

.SH KEYBOARD
Ctrl+W closes the current tab. Super+W closes the focused browser or model-preview
window. DomeD leaves Ctrl+W to applications and uses Super+W for window closing.
